# Code Quality Rules

Use TypeScript strict mode.

Avoid:
- any
- duplicated code
- huge files
- huge functions
- business logic in controllers or components
- hardcoded strings repeated everywhere
- magic numbers
- unused imports
- commented dead code

Prefer:
- small functions
- clear names
- shared constants
- reusable helpers
- typed DTOs
- typed API responses
- clean folder structure
- readable error messages

Before finishing a task:
- run lint
- run type-check
- run tests if available
- update related types
- update README or docs if setup changed
